      <section class="tg-part" id="part-2" aria-labelledby="part-2-h">
        <div class="tg-part__head">
          <span class="tg-part__kicker">Part II of Five</span>
          <h2 class="tg-part__title" id="part-2-h">The Theological Sprawl: Where Numbers 16 Goes</h2>
          <p class="tg-part__intro">Numbers 16 is unusually generative because it does not raise one doctrinal
        question; it raises the question that sits underneath a dozen others. Korah's
        challenge forces a decision about <em>what kind of thing holiness is</em> — and
        nearly every downstream debate is an application of that one decision. This part
        traces the branches, and at each one marks where the tradition actually divides
        and what the text can carry.</p>
          <blockquote class="tg-part__verse"><p>And he stood between the dead and the living, and the plague was stopped.</p>
        <cite><a class="ref" data-ref="Numbers 16:48">Numbers 16:48</a></cite></blockquote>
        </div>
