      <section class="tg-part" id="part-4" aria-labelledby="part-4-h">
        <div class="tg-part__head">
          <span class="tg-part__kicker">Part IV of Five</span>
          <h2 class="tg-part__title" id="part-4-h">The Answer Given: Church, Community, Mission, Message, and Works</h2>
          <p class="tg-part__intro">The first three parts were largely diagnostic. This one turns from diagnosis to
        construction. Korah asked a question — <em>may I draw near?</em> — and the New
        Testament answers it, then builds an entire ecclesiology, mission, and ethic on the
        answer. The connection is not homiletical decoration: the specific vocabulary of
        Numbers 16 recurs in the New Testament at precisely the load-bearing points.</p>
          <blockquote class="tg-part__verse"><p>See, here is water! What prevents me from being baptised?</p>
        <cite><a class="ref" data-ref="Acts 8:36">Acts 8:36</a></cite></blockquote>
        </div>
<nav class="tg-toc tg-toc--sticky" aria-label="Part contents">
